 "doc": "AUTH-E1 post-hoc analyses requested in the ChatGPT round-2 review (docs/auth/discussion_20261124/ROUND2_ChatGPT_outline.md),\nwritten after the one-time E1 test read; the E1 STOP verdict is not re-decided here.  Frozen models only, no refit.\n\nG8  zero-training baseline: the kept end with the highest QuantSeq signal (feature log_quant_signal = log1p of the max\n    over the three replicates); ties -> nearest.\nG9  high-quality molecule labels: MAPQ >= 30, soft clip <= 30 nt at each end, TALON fA (fraction A downstream) <= 0.5;\n    each read assigned to at most one candidate end (the nearest within +-100 bp); groups rebuilt with the same rules\n    (>= 1 end with >= 2 reads, >= 1 end with 0, cov >= 10); ends with exactly 1 read counted separately.\nG10 signal-matched hard pairs: same TSS, one supported end (>= 2) and one zero-link end, QuantSeq signals within 2x,\n    ends > 200 bp apart, cov >= 30; pairwise accuracy of G8 / E2 / E3 / E4 (higher score on the supported end).\nG11 the same candidates at locus level: S50 match to an AUTH truth lnc locus vs molecule support; what the frozen AUTH\n    model (E3) and E2 pick.\nAlso: per-chromosome group statistics (groups, candidates, supported ends, depth, top-2 signal ratio).\n",
